 Claude generated something **useful**, but it is currently a **mixed registry**, not a clean LinkML-ready model.

The problem is that it mixes **ontology**, **edge schema**, **source-pipeline decisions**, **validation rules**, **classification rules**, and **materialisation policy** in the same conceptual layer. For implementation, you must split them.

in files                                                                                                                                                                              | What is wrong / risky                                                                                                                     | How it should be                                                                                            | Why                                                                                                |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ontology_registry_federated` contains classes like `HumanAccount`, `ServiceAccount`, `BatchAccount`, `AADIdentity`, `DirectoryPerson`, `BU`, `Table`, `Database`, `CMDBRecord`, `ApplicationService` | This is useful, but it mixes **canonical ontology** with `M1/M2 pipeline`, `materialize`, `abstract/active`, and source-specific ID rules | Keep this as the basis for **LinkML classes**, but remove pipeline-specific logic from the class definition | LinkML schema should define the canonical model, not whether M1 or M2 produced the node            |
| Classes like `HumanUser`, `HumanUserOM`, `BatchAccountOM`, `ServiceAccount`, `SystemUserAccount`, `InteractiveServiceAccount`                                                                         | Too many platform-specific subtypes may explode the model                                                                                 | Use one canonical `Account` class with properties: `account_class`, `account_subtype`, `origin_platform`    | Easier validation, fewer duplicated node labels, cleaner graph queries                             |
| Edge file has `edge_label`, `source_vertex`, `target_vertex`, `semantic_layer`, `pipeline`, `materialize_policy`, `assertion_status`, `evidence_class`, `cardinality`                                 | This is actually very good, but not all of it belongs in LinkML classes                                                                   | Split into: **edge schema** in LinkML + **edge policy** in a separate YAML/table                            | LinkML should define allowed edge types; policy decides if/when to materialise them                |
