# What should go into LinkML vs outside LinkML

| Concept                                                                             |                    Put in LinkML? |          Put outside LinkML? | Why                                                                   |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------: | ---------------------------: | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `Account`, `Table`, `Database`, `CI`, `ApplicationService`, `DirectoryPerson`, `BU` |                               Yes |                           No | These are canonical graph classes                                     |
| `HumanAccount`, `ServiceAccount`, `BatchAccount`                                    |  Maybe, but better as enums first |                        Maybe | Safer to use `Account.account_subtype` instead of too many subclasses |
| `account_subtype = Human / SU / ISA_TD / ISA_OM / Batch`                            |                      Yes, as enum |                           No | This is taxonomy                                                      |
| `source_record_id`, `evidence_id`                                                   |      Yes, required slots on edges |                           No | Must be enforced for provenance                                       |
| `M1`, `M2`, `Both`                                                                  |                      No, not core |                          Yes | Pipeline-specific metadata                                            |
| `materialize_policy`                                                                |                No, not core model |                          Yes | Decides physical graph output                                         |
| `VAL-001` to `VAL-028`                                                              |     Some simple ones yes; most no |                          Yes | Business validation is custom Python                                  |
| Prefix rules like `SU`, `ACOE`, `ISA`                                               |                                No |                          Yes | Classification logic before schema validation                         |
| `canonical_id_rule`                                                                 | Include as description/annotation | Also keep in `id_rules.yaml` | Important for dedup                                                   |
| Source freshness rules                                                              |                                No |                          Yes | Pipeline validator, not ontology                                      |
| `assertion_status`                                                                  |              Yes as enum/property |               Also in policy | Useful to distinguish accepted/conditional/pending facts              |

