# One clean example

Instead of this as many node labels:

```text
ServiceAccount
SystemUserAccount
InteractiveServiceAccount
BatchAccount
BatchAccountOM
NHIAccount
```

Use:

```yaml
Account:
  slots:
    - account_id
    - account_name
    - account_class
    - account_subtype
    - origin_platform
```

Example values:

```yaml
account_id: account:td:SVC_ACCOUNT.BURBS157
account_name: SVC_ACCOUNT.BURBS157
account_class: technical
account_subtype: service_su
origin_platform: td
```

Then your classification rules decide:

```text
if username starts with SU / SUTB / SUAL / SUGA:
    account_subtype = service_su

if username starts with ACOE / ISA:
    account_subtype = service_isa_td

if batch prefix PU / BU / TU / OU:
    account_subtype = batch_td
```

Then LinkML validates:

```text
service_su is allowed
td is allowed
technical is allowed
```

