# summary

| Part                 | Verdict                                                                                         |
| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Ontology registry    | mixed with pipeline metadata                                    |
| Edge schema          | keep it, but split schema vs policy                                                |
| Federated notes      | should become source/pipeline policy, not core ontology                             |
| Validation rules     | implement as custom validator, not mostly LinkML                                      |
| Classification rules | implement as deterministic classification layer before validation                         |
| flaw                 | mixed in one conceptual layer                                                          |
| to be corrected      | Split into LinkML model + classification rules + validation rules + edge policy + source policy |

The clean version is: **LinkML defines what a valid canonical graph object is. classification and validation rules decide how raw M1/M2/source data becomes those canonical graph objects.**
